ive crash diet  there's a good chance that you would  gain back  even more if this extremely low calorie  miserable meal plan wasn't enough to  steer you away from all in perhaps the  next few points will  reason number two to run for the hills  are the unqualified  coaches so neither teddy or the  accountability coaches  have any background or specialized  training in nutrition and fitness  which is quite apparent by their insane  meal plan  because no credible nutrition  professional would approve that crap  and while i appreciate the transparency  of providing this information  on their website the lack of expertise  alone is a major red flag  having an interest in health and fitness  does not make somebody  qualified to dole out advice  on the subject and it's one thing if the  biggest problem  was just that people would waste their  money on crap advice and maybe wouldn't  lose weight or nothing would happen  but said crap advice can actually be  super dangerous as it clearly is  in this situation in my opinion all in  reads like a hollywood how-to for  disordered eating  so whether it is this program or any  other weight loss program  you should not be taking nutrition or  fitness advice from  somebody with no credible expertise hard  stop  number three is the excessive  weight tracking you're required to do so  weight loss is  essentially the only measure of success  for the all-in program  and is tracked through daily weigh-ins  they also have a no bullsh approach when  it comes to their daily weigh-ins  as some clients have reported being told  to pack a scale for a few days of travel  because there are no excuses  honestly that is so [ __ ]  up well i can understand the expectation  to regularly weigh yourself as part of a  weight loss program  there is absolutely no need to weigh  yourself  every single day or to even take  pictures of yourself  in fact weighing yourself daily can  actually lead to  weight fixation body dissatisfaction and  anxiety  espec